        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(memory): add excludePaths option to memorySearch config",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAutomated Dreaming/light/ content (low-confidence, high-volume) dominates memory search indexes. In our observed instance, `memory/dreaming/light/` accounts for **79% (179.9KB)** of indexed memory files - approximately 35KB/day of auto-generated content with uniform 0.58 confidence scores. This severely degrades memory search signal-to-noise ratio.\n\nUsers need a way to keep these files on disk (they're still useful for Dreaming) but exclude them from search indexing.\n\n## Solution\n\nNew `memorySearch.excludePaths` field accepts workspace-relative glob patterns:\n\n```json5\n{\n  agents: {\n    defaults: {\n      memorySearch: {\n        excludePaths: [\"memory/dreaming/light\", \"memory/archive/**\"],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\nPatterns are matched with **minimatch** (existing project dependency) against workspace-relative paths inside `memory/` and `extraPaths`.\n\n**Scope note:** `excludePaths` currently only affects the **builtin** memory search indexing backend. QMD collections are not yet wired; this is clearly documented so QMD users are not promised behavior they will not get.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n- **Filtering order**: `excludePaths` runs *after* `shouldSkipRootMemoryAuxiliaryPath` - built-in auxiliary-path filtering (e.g. `.openclaw-repair`) has higher priority\n- **Path matching**: workspace-relative (e.g. `memory/dreaming/light`), not absolute\n- **Glob support**: full minimatch wildcards (`**`, `*`, etc.)\n- **Plain directory prefix**: passing a directory path like `memory/dreaming/light` (no glob chars) automatically matches all files under that directory\n- **Backward compatible**: not passing `excludePaths` leaves behavior unchanged\n- **CLI diagnostics**: `memory status` intentionally does NOT apply excludePaths - diagnostics should see all files\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/config/types.tools.ts` - type definition\n- `src/config/zod-schema.agent-runtime.ts` - zod validation\n- `src/config/schema.help.ts` - help text\n- `src/config/schema.labels.ts` - UI label\n- `src/agents/memory-search.ts` - resolve in mergeConfig\n- `packages/memory-host-sdk/src/host/internal.ts` - core filtering logic with prefix + glob matching\n- `extensions/memory-core/src/memory/manager-sync-ops.ts` - pass through from config\n- `packages/memory-host-sdk/src/host/internal.test.ts` - unit tests\n- `docs/reference/memory-config.md` - documentation\n- `src/config/schema.help.quality.test.ts` - help key verification\n\n## Evidence\n\nUnit tests cover:\n- Exact directory path excludes files (`memory/dreaming/light`)\n- Glob wildcard excludes directories (`memory/archive/**`)\n- Empty/missing `excludePaths` returns all files (backward compat)\n- Excluded paths are tested alongside non-excluded paths to confirm specificity\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\n```\nnpm test -- packages/memory-host-sdk/src/host/internal.test.ts\n```\n\n**Result: 12/12 tests passed** ?\n\nManual `filterMinimatch` validation: **6/6 scenarios passed** ?\n\n| Scenario | Expected | Result |\n|----------|----------|--------|\n| Exact dir match (`memory/dreaming/light`) | Excluded | ? |\n| Glob wildcard (`memory/archive/**`) | Excluded | ? |\n| Non-matching path retained | Included | ? |\n| Empty excludePaths | All retained | ? |\n| Mixed excluded + retained | Correct split | ? |\n| Plain prefix w/o glob chars | Treated as dir prefix | ? |\n\nBackward compat: empty `excludePaths` retains all files ?\n\nEnvironment: Node.js v24.16.0, minimatch 10.2.5, Windows. CI check runs confirm no regressions.\n",
        "branch": "feature/memory-search-exclude-paths",
